*.log
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# --- sim harness ---------------------------------------------------------
# `sim/` results are append-only EVIDENCE (CLAUDE.md). Raw per-corner ngspice
# output (`corners/<record-id>/<corner-id>.log`) used to be re-admitted here and
# committed; since issue #636 new runs store those bytes in the fleet artifact
# store (`klt artifact put`) and commit only a manifest under
# manifests/artifacts/ -- so the blanket `*.log` above now applies to new
# corner logs again, and CI (scripts/check_artifact_manifests.py) fails if one
# is committed anyway. Logs of runs recorded BEFORE #636 are already tracked and
# stay where they are (ignore rules never affect a tracked file).
!sim/smoke_test/smoke_test.log

# Staging tree for a run's evidence bytes between the simulation and
# `klt artifact put` (covered by `sim/.work/` below; never committed).

# Derived artifacts: regenerated on every run, never evidence.
sim/.work/
sim/pdk.local.json
sim/smoke_test/pdk_include.spice
sim/smoke_test/smoke_test.spice

# `klt pex`'s own scratch dir (docs/cli/pex.md --outdir default: a `.klt/pex/`
# directory next to whatever GDS it ran against). issue #173's
# run_pex_comparator.py always redirects --outdir into a /tmp scratch dir it
# cleans up itself, so this should never populate from the documented
# reproduction path -- ignored defensively in case of a manual `klt pex`
# invocation without --outdir.
layout/**/.klt/
design/netlist/

# `klt synthesize`/`klt equiv`'s own scratch dir (docs/cli/synthesize.md /
# docs/cli/equiv.md: `.klt/synthesize/` and `.klt/equiv/` next to the request
# file) -- `design/sar-logic/flow/synth_sar_ctrl.py` always copies the
# artifacts it cares about (netlist, .ys script, JSON request/response) into
# its own committed `reports/`/`netlist/` dirs, so this scratch tree is
# regenerated on every run, never evidence.
design/sar-logic/flow/**/.klt/
